1. Data copied from OpenRA's mods/ra, mods/common and mods/ra/maps at commit
   b6fc03fcfaef1277592bbd4cbc7d44dd85219902 (data/CATALOG.md names each
   source): everything under

     data/source/

   and the files generated from it by the tools in tools/ (each says so in
   its header or in data/CATALOG.md):

     data/actors.json
     data/weapons.json
     data/CATALOG.md
     engine/rules.json
     engine/render.json
     apps/game/js/content/tables.js
     apps/game/js/content/render-facts.js
     apps/game/js/oramap/tables.js
     apps/game/js/openra-hotkeys.js
     apps/game/js/audio/catalog-data.js
     apps/game/missions/
     packages/protocol/src/coop-missions.js

   The mission maps' authors are named in each map.yaml under
   data/source/missions/maps/ and in the generated mission files.

2. Decoders for the original game's file formats, whose algorithms follow
   OpenRA's loaders (OpenRA.Mods.Cnc and OpenRA.Mods.Common: ShpTDLoader,
   ShpD2Loader, TmpRALoader, TmpTDLoader, LCWCompression,
   RLEZerosCompression, AudReader, WestwoodCompressedReader, ImaAdpcmReader,
   VqaVideo, MixFile, BlowfishKeyProvider, ImmutablePalette and
   PlayerColorPalette, DefaultSpriteSequence, CursorManager):

     apps/game/js/content/shp.js
     apps/game/js/content/vqa.js
     apps/game/js/content/palette.js
     apps/game/js/content/sequences.js
     apps/game/js/content/cursors.js
     apps/game/js/audio/aud.js
     apps/game/js/audio/mix.js
     apps/game/js/audio/mixkey.js

3. Game logic. The simulation in engine/ and the game client in apps/game/
   reimplement OpenRA's Red Alert behaviour (traits, activities, the bot
   modules, the Lua mission API); comments name the OpenRA classes they
   follow.

No files of the original Command & Conquer: Red Alert (Westwood Studios,
Electronic Arts) are part of this repository: players load the game's
graphics, sounds and movies from their own copy in the browser.

Third-party code compiled into or bundled with the shipped site (Rust
